/-!
# Block division and rank specialization

Three algebraic tools for the rational hitting lists. Bivariate polynomials embed injectively
into Hahn series over the lexicographically ordered group `QuantumLift.Exponents = ℤ ×ₗ ℤ`.
A square block matrix over a division ring `D`, flattened through a faithful matrix
representation `D →+* Matrix κ κ E`, is either invertible or loses at least `|κ|` in rank
(block elimination). Finally, specializing the entries of a matrix along a `K`-algebra map
`P →ₐ[K] K` cannot raise its rank over any field into which `P` embeds.

## Main definitions

* `Rational.PolynomialHahn.exponent`, `Rational.PolynomialHahn.variableSeries`,
  `Rational.PolynomialHahn.embed`: bivariate polynomials as Hahn series over `ℤ ×ₗ ℤ`.
* `Rational.BlockDivision.blockEmbedding`, `Rational.BlockDivision.kernelRows`: the entrywise
  extension of a matrix representation of `D` to square block matrices over `D` and the
  induced kernel-row map.

## Main results

* `Rational.PolynomialHahn.charZero`: Hahn series over a characteristic-zero ring have
  characteristic zero (a scoped instance, available after `open Rational.PolynomialHahn`).
* `Rational.PolynomialHahn.embed_injective`: the Hahn-series embedding is injective.
* `Rational.BlockDivision.rank_gap`: a block-embedded matrix is invertible or has rank at most
  `(|m| - 1) * |κ|`.
* `Rational.BlockDivision.isUnit_of_rank_gt`: rank above `(|m| - 1) * |κ|` forces invertibility.
* `Rational.RankSpecialization.rank_le`: specialization cannot raise the generic rank.

## References

* Adapted from OpenAI's formalization [OpenAI2026RationalHitting] at revision
  adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a (file
  lean/OAI/Computability/RationalHitting/BlockDivision.lean), via the complexitylib port
  [Schlesinger2026RationalHitting] at revision add0aca8ee0d71e68969f2cb45cf91554a50f787.
-/

