/-!
# Integer form of the regular lift

The generator's rational matrices are regular representations of matrices over the cyclotomic
field `CyclotomicRing.R e`. Every regular-representation entry of a cyclotomic monomial is `0`
or `±1`, so after clearing the common denominator `2 ^ (e + 1)` each lifted matrix entry is an
explicit signed sum of integer monomials. This file defines that integer formula, proves it
agrees with the rational lift, and bounds its entries. The integer matrices are computable and
feed the executable generator.

## Main definitions

* `Rational.CyclotomicRing.signedEntry`: the signed regular-representation coefficient of a
  power of the root of unity.
* `Rational.IntegralTest.full`, `Rational.IntegralTest.padded`: integer Taylor test matrices.
* `Rational.IntegralLift.entry`: the integer formula for a denominator-cleared lift entry.
* `Rational.Generator.coordinate`: the fixed row-major block coordinate.
* `Rational.Generator.integerTest`: the integer test matrices indexed by residues.
* `Rational.Generator.integralLift`: the denominator-cleared integer lift matrices.

## Main results

* `Rational.IntegralLift.entry_spec`: the integer formula computes the scaled rational entry.
* `Rational.Generator.U_cast`: the integer lift is the scaled rational lift.
* `Rational.Generator.U_bound`: an explicit bound on the integer entries.
* `Rational.Generator.tupleAt_integer`: the generated tuples are normalized integer lifts.

## References

* Adapted from OpenAI's formalization [OpenAI2026RationalHitting] at revision
  adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a (file
  lean/OAI/Computability/RationalHitting/IntegralLift.lean), via the complexitylib port
  [Schlesinger2026RationalHitting] at revision add0aca8ee0d71e68969f2cb45cf91554a50f787.
-/

