/-! # Presentation-independent program syntax of the solver helpers

Every helper program is parametrised by a macro package `M : FieldMacros F r`, but its *code*
depends on `M` only through the eight macro programs.  `CodeEq M₁ M₂` says those eight programs
coincide; the congruence theorems below then show that each helper produces literally the same
`Com` for `M₁` and `M₂`.  Since the concrete package `fieldMacros F` has field-independent code
(`fieldMacros_codeEq`), the compiled program of every helper is the same `Com` for every
presentation `F` — the "static dummy presentation" statement, for all `F` at once.  Recursive
helpers (static lists, expression trees) are handled by structural induction.
