/-!
# Transport lemmas for concrete field workspaces

The bounded solver repeatedly runs fixed programs in the canonical field
workspace and restores that workspace from a private array bank. These lemmas
isolate the two routine facts needed by that composition: a slot invariant may
be restricted to a prefix, and it may be transported across a state with the
same field-layout registers and field arrays.
