/-!
# The prologue of the multiprecision translation

`prologue` reads the length-prefixed input into the buffer `#in`, measures its bit size `n` and
largest word size `mb`, and computes the limb parameters `κ = mb + C1 (size n + 1) + K0`,
`β = 2 ^ κ`, `U = cU (n + 1) ^ DU`, `L = U / κ + 1`, `κ L` and the big constant `#KLB`.
`prologue_tstate`: from the target's initial state (array lengths `tgtExt`), the prologue reaches a
state holding the source's initial state (`TState`). Also: `BigStepB.mono` (bounds can be raised).
-/

