/-!
# Uniform normalized banks

`ubankCom M q w` is one literal `Com`, the same for every `n, m, K, F`: the dimensions are the
runtime values of the registers `w.nR = n`, `w.mR = m`.  It zero-fills the bank region
`[L, (m+1)·L)` (`N = n+1+m`, `L = 5+N+m·N`) by a runtime loop of constant loads, then runs a
loop over `k < m·m` with `j = k / m`, `i = k % m` that writes, in bank `j` at `(j+1)·L`, the
query one at `5+n`, the identity one at coordinate `n+1+i` of row `i`, the pivot one at
coordinate `n` of row `i` when `i = j`, and copies column `i` of the matrix (slots
`5+i·n, …`) into the first `n` coordinates of row `i`.  Finally `q.N := N`, `q.n := n+1`,
`q.c := m`.  Claude lane, 2026-10-02.
-/

